{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Root cause (proven 2026-10-30, worktree .rebar/worktrees/fix-test-isolation-jira-project, evidence .rebar/scratch/hammer-main/). The earlier cross-worker on-disk hypothesis is REFUTED: the failure is deterministic at collection time and needs no concurrency.\n\nObservation: a probe plugin wrapping compose_operation_snapshot showed JIRA_PROJECT was UNSET in os.environ during every failing call, and JIRA_URL was the host's real value, not the conftest's example.atlassian.net. A pytest_runtest_call hook showed `_default_jira_project in item.fixturenames == False` for all 235 tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate items on every worker (run2/call-*.jsonl). The 22 failures are just the subset that needs jira.project.\n\nMinimal deterministic repro (collect-only, -n 0):\n  pytest --co tests/unit/reconciler/test_lock_steal.py tests/unit/test_raw_git_write_lint.py tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_once.py\n  -> orchestrate items lack the reconciler conftest autouse fixtures (False 7). Dropping the middle arg, or replacing it with tests/interfaces/store, restores them (True 7).\nNode identity check: that run builds TWO Package objects for tests/unit/reconciler (id 4444005424 for the first arg, 4445891376 for the third).\n\n- Writer: pytest 9.1.1 Session.collect. A file argument directly under tests/unit (test_raw_git_write_lint.py or test_last_pass_backoff_jitter_paediatric.py) re-collects the tests/unit Dir with handle_dupes=False (_pytest/main.py:968), creating a fresh Package node for tests/unit/reconciler.\n- Shared state: FixtureManager._pending_conftests (_pytest/fixtures.py:1789-1802). A conftest's fixtures are parsed once, bound to the FIRST Directory node object for its path, then popped.\n- Reader: getfixtureinfo/_getautousenames for items under the second Package node finds no autouse names, so _default_jira_project and _sandbox_repo_root never run, and compose_operation_snapshot sees no JIRA_PROJECT.\nUpstream: pytest-dev/pytest#14635 (dupes #14964, #14971, #15071), fixed by PR #14645 \"deduplicate Directory nodes on re-collection\", released in pytest 9.2.0 (2026-10-27, changelog entry #14635). Why serial runs and file pairs passed: none of those argument lists put a tests/unit-level file between two tests/unit/reconciler args.\n\nFix: pyproject dev extra pytest>=8,!=9.1.0,!=9.1.1 and uv.lock pytest 9.1.1 -> 9.2.0. Regression test tests/unit/test_pytest_interleaved_conftest_args.py rebuilds the argument shape in a throwaway project and runs the installed pytest.\nResults:\n- Regression test on pytest 9.1.1 (main lock): FAILED; inner run reported 'FAILED tests/unit/pkg/sub/test_second.py ... 1 failed, 2 passed'.\n- Regression test on pytest 9.2.0 (fix): 1 passed.\n- Observation's -n 4 command on main: 22 failed, 2100 passed (run1, run2). On the fix: exit 0, 2122 passed, 13 skipped (run4); the collect probe shows orchestrate True 235.\n- make lint and make typecheck: pass. 17 related test files (nested-pytest, isolation, CI-parity, extras-parity, advisory): 262 passed."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793399012255530001,"uuid":"a06d98a8-89b9-48d7-b963-f88f52a450f6"}